ASoC: codecs: wcd937x: reset the codec when its SoundWire devices go away

When the SoundWire controllers behind a WCD937x unbind (on SM4375 when
the ADSP restarts and takes the LPASS macros with it), the codec's
SoundWire devices are deleted and come back with fresh register caches at
the defaults, while the codec itself keeps the values it had. The caches
then skip writes the codec still needs: after an ADSP restart the speaker
path through AUX gives one loud click and no sound.

Reset the codec when the component master unbinds, so that it starts from
its defaults like the caches.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/wcd937x.c b/sound/soc/codecs/wcd937x.c
index 08fb404e5..0c17f6dc2 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/wcd937x.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/wcd937x.c
@@ -2916,6 +2916,12 @@ static void wcd937x_unbind(struct device *dev)
 	mutex_destroy(&wcd937x->micb_lock);
 	put_device(wcd937x->txdev);
 	put_device(wcd937x->rxdev);
+	/*
+	 * The SoundWire devices come back with new register caches, at their defaults (after a DSP
+	 * restart unbinds the SoundWire controllers, say): put the codec back to its defaults too,
+	 * or the caches skip writes the codec still needs and the outputs come up wrong.
+	 */
+	wcd937x_reset(wcd937x);
 }
 
 static const struct component_master_ops wcd937x_comp_ops = {
